      "severity": "important",
      "category": "correctness",
      "title": "Override quotes a phrase the system prompt never uses",
      "description": "The override tells the model \"where it says 'what this change introduced'\", but the system prompt's actual wording is \"Anything this diff did not introduce\" (prompt.ts:94) and \"keep only what the changed lines introduce\" (prompt.ts:165). Since no rule matches the quoted string, the model has to guess which rule is being carved out — the exact ambiguity this change exists to remove. The Scope discipline section (\"you have drifted into reviewing the file instead of the change\") is also left untouched, and it pushes in the same suppressing direction.",
      "suggestion": "Consider anchoring the exception to the wording that is actually in the system prompt, and naming the scope-discipline rule too, so both suppressing rules are covered.",
